chain.json: accounts read back (getAccount / getProgramIds over JSON-RPC) from the PUBLIC
LEZ testnet, https://testnet.lez.logos.co. They were captured right after lez-multisig's own
e2e suite (e2e_tests/tests/e2e_multisig.rs, BLOCK_WAIT_SECS=60) passed there.

The program: lez-multisig ported to SPEL v0.7.0 / LEZ v0.2.4, with the lez-multisig#40 fix
(logos-co/lez-multisig#45, which includes #41). It was deployed to the testnet on 2026-09-24:
  ImageID    2ced3d301a4d1cd5db6cad9c428b9f3463155073f8bacf73179c6ea6536de4c7
  deploy tx  61a7abe2cfeddeae3cd54f23317f50e984eb331f420d013210e7eabcc896faa0 (block 23405)

The testnet's built-in program image ids equal a v0.2.4 build's, byte for byte.

The run is the same as in vectors/lez-multisig-v024:
- a 2-of-3 multisig;
- proposal 1 initializes the vault's token holding through a ChainedCall into the token
  program;
- 500 tokens fund the vault;
- proposal 2 transfers 200 to a recipient. First, an execute that substitutes the recipient
  was refused on the live chain. Then the approved execute landed.

Field encoding:
- `id` fields are the base58 account ids decoded to hex;
- `program_owner` and the image ids are the [u32; 8] words as little-endian bytes.

Captured 2026-09-24.
